        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0370" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg300"/>

                <head>F. W. Seward to Mr. McCook</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 26.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 27, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Mr. Rouse’s despatch No. 22, of the 7th of
                    February last, relative to the case of the discharged seamen of the Blue Jacket,
                    has been received. It seems from this communication that a claim for damages on
                    account of the discharges of the seamen has been presented to the consulate.</p>
                <p>Whatever may ultimately be the opinion of this government as to the right of
                    jurisdiction in the matter assumed by the Hawaiian courts, it is clear that as
                    the captain neglected to appeal to the supreme court from the adverse decision
                    of the court below, the claim for damages referred to cannot be ascertained, and
                    need not be presented by you to that government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward M. McCook,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
